# Terraform
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# The lock file is ignored here because every lab directory is an ephemeral
# practice environment and pinning providers across dozens of them adds noise.
# In a real project you should commit .terraform.lock.hcl, so that every
# collaborator and every CI run resolves the exact same provider versions.
# That distinction is itself exam material.

# tflocal writes this when it injects LocalStack endpoint overrides
localstack_providers_override.tf

# LocalStack container working directory
.localstack/

# Learner scratch space
work/

# Environment and secrets
.env

# tfvars files routinely hold credentials, so they are ignored by default.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Reference solutions and lab starter files are the exception. They hold only
# fictional values and are the point of the repository, so they must be
# committed. Anything you write under work/ stays ignored.
!solutions/**/*.tfvars
!problems/**/*.tfvars

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
